---
import ServiceSection from "../../components/ServiceSection.astro";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import ServiceLayout from "../../layouts/ServiceLayout.astro";
---

<Layout>
	<ServiceLayout
		eyebrow="Websites & integrations"
		title="Websites & custom integrations"
		intro="Connected digital experiences that make all of your tools more useful."
		highlights={[
			"Product design & architecture",
			"Web design & development",
			"Systems integration",
			"Ongoing optimization",
		]}
	>
		<ServiceSection heading="Digital products built around real workflows">
			<p>
				Nightmare Software creates websites, internal tools, and customer-facing
				applications around how people actually work. That starts with
				understanding the users, decisions, handoffs, and constraints behind a
				request—not just selecting a framework or reproducing a visual concept.
				Interfaces are designed to make important actions clear, reduce
				unnecessary steps, and present the right information at the right time.
			</p>
			<p>
				For websites and customer apps, we focus on useful experiences as well
				as polished presentation. That can include clear content structures,
				accessible interactions, account areas, forms, search, notifications,
				and responsive behavior across devices. For internal tools, the emphasis
				may be different: efficient data entry, practical dashboards, role-based
				access, approvals, reporting, and workflows that fit existing
				operational processes instead of forcing teams into a generic system.
			</p>
		</ServiceSection>
		<ServiceSection heading="Systems that work with the tools you already use">
			<p>
				Many software projects depend on more than the application itself.
				Nightmare Software connects new experiences to the systems a company
				already relies on, including business platforms, databases, payment
				services, communication tools, and third-party APIs. The work may
				involve mapping data between systems, handling authentication and
				permissions, synchronizing records, processing webhooks, or creating a
				focused interface over several disconnected tools.
			</p>
			<p>
				Integrations are planned with the realities of production use in mind.
				That means considering incomplete data, duplicate events, failed
				requests, changing API behavior, and what happens when a connected
				service is unavailable. Where appropriate, we can separate integration
				logic from the user interface, add logging and operational visibility,
				and define clear boundaries so the system remains understandable and
				maintainable as requirements change.
			</p>
			<p>
				The result is technology chosen for a concrete purpose: helping
				customers complete tasks, helping staff work more effectively, or
				helping systems exchange reliable information. Nightmare Software can
				work from an early concept, improve an existing product, or extend the
				capabilities of a company's current stack without treating replacement
				as the default answer.
			</p>
		</ServiceSection>
	</ServiceLayout>
</Layout>
